\8t+16-15t^3\\\\-6t^4-t^2-6t-8\\end{bmatrix}.$$ Differentiate each component to obtain $$(\\mathbf f\\times\\mathbf g)'(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20\\\\8-45t^2\\\\-24t^3-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}.$$" 13194139536108 false] [17592186115679 1145 "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6t \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4t \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6t & 1 & 0 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}6t & 0 \\\\ t+2 & 5t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}6t & 1 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & t+4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4t & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}t+4 & 8 \\\\ -4t & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2} & 8 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2} & t+4 \\\\ 1 & -4t\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383976 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1089 "q-128137" 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1100 "Find the value of $(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}$ at $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3(t+1)},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1113 #uuid "d9ac2eaf-d9c7-536c-9c41-51336e100c20" 13194139536108 true] [17592186383975 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-3{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3(t+1)}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(0)-3g(0))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(0)-3{g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+1}},\\,3(0)^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{0+1}⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3(0+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383977 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383978 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383979 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383980 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383981 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536108 true] [17592186383976